{
  "id": "ecd938e3-be5a-41f4-a4f1-5689bcbcf18e",
  "page_title": "Quickstart: Generate images with Azure OpenAI Service using PowerShell",
  "page_description": "Learn how to generate images with Azure OpenAI Service by using PowerShell and the endpoint and access keys for your Azure OpenAI resource.",
  "page_date": "08/29/2023",
  "chunk_title": "Output",
  "chunk_content": "Output  PowerShell requests the image from Azure OpenAI and stores the output image in the _generated_image.png_ file in your specified directory. For convenience, the full path for the file is returned at the end of the script.  The image generation APIs come with a content moderation filter. If the service recognizes your prompt as harmful content, it doesn't generate an image. For more information, see Content filtering.",
